user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 4,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_explicit_uncertainty",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text: 1 if the OP explicitly admits uncertainty or possible error about their own view/claims, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP post body; may contain later edits, which are not separated out; do not infer an initial version). Return 1 if the OP in their own voice explicitly expresses uncertainty, doubt, or admits they might be wrong about their view or claims (e.g. 'I may be wrong', 'I'm not sure', 'I could be missing something'). Exclude quoted external text, opponents' positions reported by the OP, and generic invitations to respond ('change my view') or hedging of minor details unrelated to doubt about the OP's position. Return 0 if the text is assessable and has no such explicit statement. Return null if argument is missing or empty/unparseable."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 30,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_modest_uncertain_epistemic_markers",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text (post body, excluding quoted external text and marked edits): 1 if the OP's stance is predominantly expressed with modest/uncertain epistemic markers, else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column. Judge the OP's own claims about their view; ignore quoted external text and edit notes (e.g., 'EDIT:'). Return 1 if the OP's central claims are mainly framed with modest, hedged or uncertain epistemic markers (e.g., 'I think', 'maybe', 'might', 'perhaps', 'I'm not sure', 'it seems', 'to my knowledge', 'could be wrong'). Return 0 if the central claims are mainly stated assertively or with high-modality markers (e.g., 'definitely', 'must', 'obviously', 'always', 'undeniably', 'objectively'), or unmarked flat assertions with no hedging. If mixed, choose by how the main thesis is framed. Return null if argument is missing, empty or unparseable. Not an validated scale; no frequency cutoff is imposed beyond the predominant framing of the main thesis."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 34,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_argument_has_explicit_uncertainty",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text: 1 if it contains at least one explicit uncertainty marker about the OP's own claims/view, else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP's post body; may contain later edits, which are not separable, and quoted text). Return 1 if the OP's own voice explicitly expresses uncertainty, hedged confidence or possibility of being wrong about their own view or claims (e.g. 'I'm not sure', 'I might be wrong', 'to my knowledge', 'I could be mistaken', 'I'm unsure', 'maybe I am missing something'). Return 0 if no such explicit marker exists. Exclude uncertainty in quoted external text, uncertainty attributed to others, generic hedges unrelated to the OP's stance (e.g. 'maybe' in hypothetical examples), and moderator/bot notices. Do not count mere invitations to challenge the view unless they state uncertainty. Return null if argument is missing or empty/unparseable."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
